      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 527417069,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Hi Philippe,\n\nif I'm not mistaken, libgcrypt 1.7.0 already supports this cipher according to https://lists.gnupg.org/pipermail/gnupg-announce/2016q2/000386.html\n\nIf this is confirmed, we should use the libgcrypt implementation as we already have a dependency on this library and not introduce a new third party one (that we would need to support on Linux, Mac and Windows).",
          "author": {
            "id": 6722527,
            "username": "pquantin",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Pascal Quantin",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9bf49edc6acae0eca821eb90309381794fb4fbea4f3fb7c2378428862ddbb430?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/pquantin"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-03-11T17:05:57.188Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-03-11T17:05:57.188Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 91730835,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 2353,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 527459591,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Hi Pascal\n\nI've try to use the libgcrypt, before using Sodium, but libgcrypt implement chacha20-poly1305 but not the IETF version.\nI use the IETF version of chacha20-poly1305 because LibOscore (with libcose) use this cipher suite.\nFor more details, see https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7539.\n\nFor me, if libgcrypt can do it, I prefer to use it.\n\nIf inserting a third party is problematic, we will wait for a new version of libgcrypt compatible.\nFor my part, I proposed this evolution because I had implemented it.\nIf it is refused, no worries!",
          "author": {
            "id": 8375613,
            "username": "Ph-S",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Philippe SURBAYROLE",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
